2
00:00:07,759 --> 00:00:10,870
Lesson 1, Bob's day at work.

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:14,089
Bob works as a manager in a furniture store.

4
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:17,469
Peter, his boss, is not happy about sales.

5
00:00:18,120 --> 00:00:20,769
Bob's new advertising campaign hasn't helped.

6
00:00:21,179 --> 00:00:23,049
Peter decides to fire him.

7
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:28,389
Bob, I hate to break the news, but our sales were down again last month.

8
00:00:28,239 --> 00:00:29,849
Down again, Peter?

9
00:00:30,320 --> 00:00:34,549
Yeah, these days everybody's shopping at our competition on a stave's furniture store.

10
00:00:34,979 --> 00:00:37,189
But everything in there costs an arm in a leg.

11
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,670
That's true. They do charge top dollar.

12
00:00:40,259 --> 00:00:43,890
And their salespeople are very strange. They really give me the creeps.

13
00:00:43,880 --> 00:00:45,969
Well, they must be doing something right over there.

14
00:00:46,079 --> 00:00:47,809
Meanwhile, we're about to go belly up.

15
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:51,990
I'm sorry to hear that. I thought my new advertising campaign would save the day.

16
00:00:52,439 --> 00:00:55,750
Let's face it, your advertising campaign was a real flop.

17
00:00:56,239 --> 00:00:58,670
Well, then I'll go back to the drawing board.

18
00:00:58,820 --> 00:01:00,629
It's too late for that. You're fired.

19
00:01:00,859 --> 00:01:02,670
What? You're giving me the axe?

20
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:06,630
Yes, I've already found a new manager. She's a sharp as a tack.

21
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:10,730
Can we even talk this over? After all, I've been working here for 10 years.

22
00:01:11,219 --> 00:01:14,350
There's no point in arguing, Bob. I've already made up my mind.

23
00:01:14,719 --> 00:01:17,670
Oh well, at least I won't have to put up with your nonsense anymore.

24
00:01:18,159 --> 00:01:20,530
Goodbye to you and goodbye to the stead and job.

25
00:01:20,819 --> 00:01:22,469
Please leave before I lose my temper.

